ci_pytest_invocation_scopes_a_path` passes it without a word. The code this replaced (`\"uv run pytest\" in stripped`, and the CI-scope guard's `uv run .*\\bpytest\\b`) did collect these forms, so this is a regression in a guard written for a defect that recurred three times. YAML authors quote a `run:` value whenever it holds `: ` or starts with a special character, so the form is ordinary. Why it broke: the boundary was set to whitespace, when the thing to exclude is a path or name character. Fix: bound the words with a class of name characters, for example `(?<![\\w./-])uv run(?![\\w./-]).*?(?<![\\w./-])pytest(?![\\w./-])`. Add a quoted line, single and double, to `test_an_invocation_with_uvs_own_options_is_still_scanned`'s fixture and watch it fail against the current pattern. Core rule: 'When you fix a defect, make inputs the fix does not know fail by name, and grep the commit for the same shape'.", "files": ["tests/test_assert_tests_ran.py", "tests/test_default_suite_ci_scope.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "Chunk 05's done-when on issue transfer is open as this bundle goes to merge", "recommendation": "Not silent: the plan's Goals log says '05: the Player's issues are transferred only after the owner sees the list; that step is the owner's turn'. But chunk 05's Done-when still lists 'The transferred issues resolve on arrt-player, and /prawduct:backlog there lists them', and this is the cumulative ready-for-merge review. Put the list of issues in the PR body so the owner rules on it at merge. Or, if the transfer is meant to follow the merge, mark that done-when as after-merge in the plan. Scope: instance.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-wave-5-split.md"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "curation.service still points to display.service for its rationale, and that file is no longer in this repository", "recommendation": "Class, bounded to deploy/. The chunk 05 sweep was keyed on `arrt-player/`, which these lines do not contain. deploy/curation.service (unchanged, so outside the subject set) still says 'Un-prefixed, for the reason spelled out in display.service', 'Absolute for the reason spelled out in display.service ... shared by both planes', 'Same reasoning as the display unit', and 'The display plane needs no such line'. A maintainer following any of these finds nothing in this tree. Nothing reads these comments, so no fix commit is wanted on their account. If the file is touched anyway, state each reason in place and delete the cross-reference. Search deploy/ for `display.service`, `display unit` and `both planes`.", "files": ["deploy/README.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "Bare-filename citations of files that left with the Player still dangle; the arrt-player: convention was applied to source paths only", "recommendation": "Scope: class. It broke because the sweep, and the plan's Done-when grep (`grep -rn \"arrt-player/\"`), keyed on the `arrt-player/` prefix, while the deploy files and findings this commit deleted are cited by bare name. Core rule 'When you retire, amend, descope or close anything, first grep the whole repo (no --include) for its nouns and OLD wording' applies, and so does 'After a scripted mass edit, verify with a method keyed on something the edit did not key on'. Members found: deploy/curation.service lines 27 and 31 ('for the reason spelled out in display.service', 'shared by both planes'). The rest are in oracle records, so the Records Pass rates them: operational-spec.md:635 tells the operator to install `deploy/journald.conf.d/10-bound-the-journal.conf` (a deleted config reference in an instruction); labels-and-surfaces.md frontmatter `governed_by: - artifact: samsung-tv-state-findings`, which record_lint did not flag; 3tears-integration-findings.md:253 has a markdown link to the deleted platform-and-dependency-findings.md; boundary-patterns.md:494/502, feeds-and-players.md:280/291, nonfunctional-requirements.md:344/428/469/1328, clients.md:135, operational-spec.md:65/756/811 and project-preferences.md:52/67 cite samsung-tv-state-findings, hdmi-output-findings, platform-and-dependency-findings or apple-platform-findings with no repository. How to bound it: take the basenames from `git diff --diff-filter=D --name-only c5e2d5e1 HEAD`, search the tracked tree outside history for them, then either prefix each survivor with `arrt-player:` as this commit did for source paths or delete the claim. A construction already exists: declare the moved names in a `retires:` list on the wave-5 decision in project-state.yaml, and record_lint's `retired-claim-survives` will find the survivors, and any later one.", "files": ["deploy/display.service", "deploy/journald.conf.d/10-bound-the-journal.conf", ".prawduct/artifacts/samsung-tv-state-findings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/platform-and-dependency-findings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/hdmi-output-findings.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/apple-platform-findings.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "note", "title": "The CI-scope test imports a private regex from another test module instead of the shared helper module", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. tests/test_default_suite_ci_scope.py does `from test_assert_tests_ran import _INVOCATION`, the only test-to-test import in any suite. The root pyproject's `pythonpath = [\"tests\"]` comment names `tests/repository.py` as the module the guards share. Moving `_INVOCATION` there and importing it from both tests removes a private-name dependency between two test files. This is cheap and worth carrying in the next commit that is already happening, not a commit of its own.", "files": ["tests/test_default_suite_ci_scope.py", "tests/test_assert_tests_ran.py"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "test_repo_hygiene.py's rewritten prose describes a deployment that is no longer the live one", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The new LIVE_UNITS comment says 'The unit that runs the server', and the module docstring now calls the manifest builder 'the only channel between the server and its Players'. But deploy/README.md \u00a7 curation.service says the unit 'has been stopped and disabled' since the server moved to the NAS container on 2026-10-02, and Players also reach the server through GET /client, heartbeat and media routes. Nothing reads this prose. When the file is next touched, make it relational (the systemd unit, for running without the container) or delete the claim. The one-entry mapping is fine as it stands.", "files": ["tests/test_repo_hygiene.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "'display plane' vocabulary and justifications survive in arrt/ beside the renamed sites", "recommendation": "Scope: class. To bound it, search `git grep -n 'display plane' -- arrt/src arrt/tools`. The diff renamed heartbeat.py's writer paragraph to 'a Player', but the same file's first docstring line still reads 'what the display plane says about itself'. Other members: observations.py, readiness.py, http/models.py, programming/display.py, static/screens/health.js, and arrt/tools/mutation_sweep.py. In mutation_sweep.py, the ROOT and serial_flags comments justify `--project` by 'the display plane is a sibling uv project', a constraint this commit removed; `--project` now serves only contract/, and neither docs/testing.md nor CLAUDE.md says so. Nothing reads any of this prose, so no edit is wanted beyond the mutation_sweep justification. Rewrite that one to name contract/ the next time the tool is touched.", "files": ["arrt/src/arrt/programming/manifest/heartbeat.py", "arrt/tools/mutation_sweep.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "README Quick start's two `cd arrt &&` lines fail if run as one sequence", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. This 